---
// G2 English edition: "How do legal dong and administrative dong differ?" (Korean original: src/guides/LegalDong.astro)
// Definitions: Local Autonomy Act arts. 7 and 9, Spatial Data Act art. 2. Counts: MOLIT legal-dong list (src/data/legal-dong-seoul.json)
// and Fill the Map's administrative-dong boundaries (svg). Which admin dong covers which legal dong: Seoul table (src/data/seoul-dong-map.json). All built by pipeline/build-geo.mjs
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import { region, svgOf, enNameOf, enDongs } from '../lib/geo';
import LEGAL from '../data/legal-dong-seoul.json';
import DONGMAP from '../data/seoul-dong-map.json';

const r = region('seoul');
const svg = svgOf('seoul');
const legalOf = (ko: string) => (LEGAL.byGu as Record<string, string[]>)[ko] ?? [];
const MAP = DONGMAP.byGu as Record<string, { adm: string; legal: string[] }[]>;
const covers = (gu: string, adm: string) => MAP[gu].find((r) => r.adm === adm)?.legal ?? [];
const sharedBy = (gu: string, legal: string) => MAP[gu].filter((r) => r.legal.includes(legal)).map((r) => r.adm);
const rows = r.items.map((it) => ({ id: it.id, ko: it.ko, legal: legalOf(it.ko).length, adm: svg.items.find((s) => s.id === it.id)!.dongs.length, dongs: svg.items.find((s) => s.id === it.id)!.dongs }))
  .sort((a, b) => b.legal - b.adm - (a.legal - a.adm));
const legalSum = rows.reduce((t, x) => t + x.legal, 0);
const admSum = rows.reduce((t, x) => t + x.adm, 0);
const max = Math.max(...rows.flatMap((x) => [x.legal, x.adm]));
const more = rows.filter((x) => x.adm > x.legal).length;
const same = rows.filter((x) => x.adm === x.legal).map((x) => enNameOf(x.id));
const row = (ko: string) => rows.find((x) => x.ko === ko)!;
const jongno = row('종로구'), junggu = row('중구'), gwanak = row('관악구');
const admRange = [Math.min(...rows.map((x) => x.adm)), Math.max(...rows.map((x) => x.adm))];
const legalRange = [Math.min(...rows.map((x) => x.legal)), Math.max(...rows.map((x) => x.legal))];
// Sentence checks (the build stops if the data changes)
if (!jongno.dongs.includes('청운효자동') || !legalOf('종로구').includes('청운동') || !legalOf('종로구').includes('효자동')) throw new Error('G2 청운효자동 예시가 데이터와 다름');
if (!['종로1가', '종로2가', '종로3가', '종로4가'].every((d) => legalOf('종로구').includes(d)) || !jongno.dongs.includes('종로1·2·3·4가동')) throw new Error('G2 종로1·2·3·4가동 예시가 데이터와 다름');
const cheongun = covers('종로구', '청운효자동'), jongro14 = covers('종로구', '종로1·2·3·4가동');
if (!['청운동', '효자동'].every((d) => cheongun.includes(d)) || !['종로1가', '종로2가', '종로3가', '종로4가'].every((d) => jongro14.includes(d))) throw new Error('G2 예시가 서울시 대응표와 다름');
const bongcheon = sharedBy('관악구', '봉천동'), sillim = sharedBy('관악구', '신림동');
const gwanakLegal = legalOf('관악구');
const gwanakOther = gwanak.dongs.filter((d) => !gwanakLegal.includes(d)).slice(0, 3);
// English name of a dong: administrative dongs come from enDongs (same order as the boundary data); legal dongs that are not
// administrative dong names are in this small table (Revised Romanization). An unknown name stops the build.
const LEGAL_EN: Record<string, string> = { '봉천동': 'Bongcheon-dong', '청운동': 'Cheongun-dong', '효자동': 'Hyoja-dong' };
const enOfDong = (x: { id: string; dongs: string[] }, ko: string) => {
  const i = x.dongs.indexOf(ko);
  const en = i >= 0 ? enDongs(x.id)[i] : LEGAL_EN[ko];
  if (!en) throw new Error(`G2 en: no English name for ${ko}`);
  return en;
};
const gwanakLegalEn = gwanakLegal.map((d) => enOfDong(gwanak, d));
const gwanakOtherEn = gwanakOther.map((d) => enOfDong(gwanak, d));
const SRC = {
  law: 'https://www.law.go.kr/법령/지방자치법',
  land: 'https://www.law.go.kr/법령/공간정보의구축및관리등에관한법률',
  bjd: 'https://www.data.go.kr/data/15063424/fileData.do',
};
---
<div class="summary">
  <b>Key points</b>
  <span>1. A legal dong (beopjeong-dong) is the original dong. Land lot numbers are given by dong and ri, so a lot-number address shows the legal dong name.</span>
  <span>2. An administrative dong (haengjeong-dong) is a dong that is run for convenience, with a community service center (jumin-senteo). It may combine legal dong or split one.</span>
  <span>3. Seoul has {legalSum} legal dong and {admSum} administrative dong. Fill the Map uses administrative dong.</span>
</div>

<h2>How the law separates the two</h2>
<p>Article 7 of the Local Autonomy Act says that the names and areas of eup, myeon and dong stay as they were, and that changes are set by ordinance. The dong that has continued this way is the legal dong. Paragraph 4 of the same article says that, for administrative efficiency and the convenience of residents, one dong may be run as two or more, or two or more dong may be run as one. These are called "administrative dong" (haengjeong-dong). Article 9 then says that, for setting up a dong office (community service center), the dong means the administrative dong.</p>
<p>For land, the legal dong is used. Article 2 of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data (called the Spatial Data Act here) defines the lot number (jibeon) as the number assigned to each parcel of land, and the area unit in which lot numbers are assigned as the dong or ri. So a lot-number address shows the legal dong, and the name of a community service center shows the administrative dong. For example, in Seoul's data, the administrative dong Cheongunhyoja-dong in Jongno-gu covers {cheongun.length} legal dong, including Cheongun-dong and Hyoja-dong. Jongno 1·2·3·4-ga-dong covers {jongro14.length} legal dong, including Jongno 1-ga to 4-ga. Only some of those names appear in the name of the administrative dong.</p>

<h2>Districts that combine, districts that split</h2>
<p>Of Seoul's 25 districts, {more} have more administrative dong than legal dong. This is because some legal dong are run as several administrative dong. On the other hand, Jongno-gu and Jung-gu have many legal dong ({jongno.legal} and {junggu.legal}), and they combine them into a few administrative dong.{same.length ? ` ${same.join(', ')} ${same.length > 1 ? 'have' : 'has'} the same number of both, but the same number does not mean the same boundaries.` : ''}</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Jongno-gu</b>: {jongno.legal} legal dong → {jongno.adm} administrative dong</li>
  <li><b>Jung-gu</b>: {junggu.legal} legal dong → {junggu.adm} administrative dong</li>
  <li><b>Gwanak-gu</b>: {gwanak.legal} legal dong ({gwanakLegalEn.join(', ')}) → {gwanak.adm} administrative dong</li>
</ul>
<div class="tbl"><table class="pair">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">District</th><th scope="col">Legal dong · Administrative dong</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{rows.map((x) => (
    <tr><td>{enNameOf(x.id)}</td><td>
      <div class="bar"><i class="b-legal" style={`width:${(x.legal / max) * 85}%`}></i><span class="num">{x.legal}</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><i class="b-adm" style={`width:${(x.adm / max) * 85}%`}></i><span class="num">{x.adm}</span></div>
    </td></tr>
  ))}</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta"><i class="key b-legal"></i>Legal dong <i class="key b-adm"></i>Administrative dong · Districts are listed starting with those that have the most legal dong compared with administrative dong.</p>

<h2>So the names can differ</h2>
<p>Gwanak-gu has only three legal dong: {gwanakLegalEn.join(', ')}. So by lot-number address, every piece of land in Gwanak-gu is in one of these three dong. But there are {gwanak.adm} community service centers, and many of their names, such as {gwanakOtherEn.join(', ')}, are not on the legal dong list. In Seoul's data, the legal dong Bongcheon-dong is shared by {bongcheon.length} administrative dong, and Sillim-dong by {sillim.length}. If the dong name of your home looks different on a lot-number address and on a community service center, it is because one is the legal dong and the other is the administrative dong.</p>

<h2>Why Fill the Map uses administrative dong</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>The dong residents visit</b>: There is a community service center in every administrative dong. The dong in the name of a community service center is the administrative dong.</li>
  <li><b>Evenly sized units for practice</b>: Each Seoul district has a similar number of administrative dong, {admRange[0]} to {admRange[1]}, but the number of legal dong varies a lot, from {legalRange[0]} to {legalRange[1]}. If we used legal dong, Jongno-gu alone would have {jongno.legal} cells.</li>
  <li><b>Boundary data</b>: There is public data that organizes administrative dong boundaries edition by edition, so changed dong can be added quickly. The current edition is the one of October 1, 2026.</li>
</ul>
<p>So every dong on the Fill the Map maps is an administrative dong. It may differ from the dong name in a lot-number address, so each <a href={href('/en/seoul/')}>Seoul district page</a> also has a table of the legal dong that each administrative dong covers.</p>
<div class="cta"><b>Try it on the map</b><a class="btn" href={href('/en/#/kr/seoul/sgg/p1')}>Start Seoul lesson 1</a></div>

<h2>Sources</h2>
<ul class="src">
  <li>National Law Information Center, <a href={SRC.law}>Local Autonomy Act</a> (Act No. 21544, in force October 15, 2026), arts. 7 and 9</li>
  <li>National Law Information Center, <a href={SRC.land}>Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data</a> (Act No. 21447, in force July 1, 2026), art. 2, items 22 and 23</li>
  <li>Number of legal dong: Public Data Portal, <a href={SRC.bjd}>Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, Legal Dongs of Korea</a> (revised July 29, 2026; no restrictions on use). We counted the dong lines for Seoul, leaving out ri.</li>
  <li>Number of administrative dong: counted from the administrative dong boundaries as of October 1, 2026.</li>
  <li>Legal dong covered by each administrative dong: Seoul Metropolitan Government, <a href={DONGMAP.source.url}>List of dong by district (Hangul and Hanja)</a> (revised August 18, 2025)</li>
</ul>


<style>
  /* Bars: ink fill = legal dong, surface color + ink border = administrative dong, square corners. Numbers 14px */
  .bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; height: 18px; margin: 3px 0; }
  .bar i { display: block; flex: none; height: 12px; min-width: 2px; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .bar .num { font-size: var(--fs-14); line-height: 18px; color: var(--ink-2); white-space: nowrap; }
  .b-legal { background: var(--ink); }
  .b-adm { background: var(--sunk); border: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .key { display: inline-block; width: 16px; height: 16px; box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0 6px 0 14px; vertical-align: -3px; border-radius: var(--r-sw); }
  .key:first-child { margin-left: 0; }
  table.pair td:last-child { width: 70%; }
</style>
